Bugfix: Avoid repeated retries for permanent errors on the same file

When using backends with flaky error handling such as `rclone`, restic retried
every permanent error (for example HTTP 416 errors when reading blobs from a
truncated pack file) up to five times per request, causing long retry loops
during commands like `repair packs`.

Restic now remembers files that already failed with a permanent error and does
not retry further permanent errors for those files, while still allowing valid
ranges of a truncated file to be read.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/5530
